        "A sailor could pass from disciplined combat to wounded dependence, exchange, captivity, or years of claims. Free Black sailors served aboard American warships and privateers, sometimes in integrated gun crews whose work was recognized in a muster while their civil standing ashore remained restricted. British ships included sailors drawn from imperial ports and maritime labor markets that did not fit a simple national pairing.",
