        "They also attached national meaning to skilled labor. Carpenters built and repaired hulls, sailmakers cut canvas, ropemakers supplied rigging, foundries cast guns, and dockyard workers kept ships available. At sea, hundreds of men handled sails, powder, shot, pumps, wounded bodies, and prisoners. The captain's name organized the report, but no captain fired a broadside alone.",
        "Constitution survived the war and later escaped destruction through preservation campaigns. Visitors can stand within a hull connected to these events, although restoration has replaced material over time. The ship is both artifact and working inheritance.",
